Feature: Create a payment

  Scenario: A card payment is authorized, and shows only the end and the expiry of the card
    When I run "create_payment" with:
      | merchant_id | amount | currency | method | idempotency_key | card                                                                                      | caller.key_kind | caller.merchant_id | now                  | event_id                             |
      | m_1         | 5000   | EUR      | card   | order-1         | {"card_number": "4242424242424242", "exp_month": 12, "exp_year": 2030, "security_code": "123"} | secret          | m_1                | 2026-11-24T10:00:00Z | 00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001 |
    Then the output is "payment_changed":
      | payment                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                         | payment_event                                                                                                                                                                                                                              |
      | {"payment_id": "pay_new000000000000000000000", "merchant_id": "m_1", "amount": 5000, "currency": "EUR", "method": "card", "status": "authorized", "captured_amount": 0, "refunded_amount": 0, "card_summary": {"brand": "visa", "last4": "4242", "exp_month": 12, "exp_year": 2030}, "created_at": "2026-11-24T10:00:00Z"} | {"event_id": "00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001", "event_type": "payment.authorized", "payment_id": "pay_new000000000000000000000", "merchant_id": "m_1", "amount": 5000, "currency": "EUR", "new_status": "authorized", "occurred_at": "2026-11-24T10:00:00Z"} |

